keywords:
  - de-identification
  - protected health information
  - HIPAA Safe Harbor
  - clinical notes
  - natural language processing
  - privacy
  - research data
abstract: >-
  Helps remove patient identifiers from typed clinical documents (Word,
  text-based PDF, Excel, CSV, plain text) on the user's own computer, and
  records what it did. Each patient's notes are read together; identifiers
  listed by the HIPAA Safe Harbor method are redacted, including in document
  metadata, comments, tracked changes and hidden sheets. Every file received
  is sorted into one of three folders (redacted with no flags, redacted with
  flagged words, not processed), with an audit trail,
  citations and a feedback report. Runs offline; a command-line tool with a small desktop
  window. Every output requires human review. Provided as is; not legal
  advice, not a certification, not a medical device, and not yet validated
  on real clinical records.
